From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx8-isi-cap: tolerate optional get_frame_interval

mxc_isi_cap_g_parm() treats any negative return from the remote
subdev's pad->get_frame_interval() call as a hard failure, including
-ENOIOCTLCMD, which simply means the sensor does not implement that
optional pad op. Sensor drivers such as ov5645 only implement
enum_mbus_code, enum_frame_size, get_fmt, set_fmt, get_selection,
enable_streams and disable_streams, so VIDIOC_G_PARM always fails
with:

  isi-capture 32e00000.isi:cap_device: failed to call get_frame_interval

Every other v4l2_subdev_call() site in this file already tolerates
-ENOIOCTLCMD from optional remote subdev ops (see
mxc_isi_source_fmt_init() and mxc_isi_cap_streamon()); apply the same
convention here so VIDIOC_G_PARM no longer fails just because the
sensor does not report an explicit frame interval.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate NXP proprietary driver
---
 drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c
index 053e1b4c06b1..c1b024f1a2d5 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx8-isi-cap.c
@@ -1077,7 +1077,7 @@ static int mxc_isi_cap_g_parm(struct file *file, void *fh,
 		return -ENODEV;
 
 	ret = v4l2_subdev_call(sd, pad, get_frame_interval, NULL, &ival);
-	if (ret < 0) {
+	if (ret < 0 && ret != -ENOIOCTLCMD) {
 		dev_err(&isi_cap->pdev->dev, "failed to call get_frame_interval\n");
 		return ret;
 	}
-- 
